## 7. Exit Code Semantics & CI Integration

The test suite concludes execution with standard POSIX exit status:
```javascript
if (failedChecks > 0) {
  console.log(`\n${C.red}${C.bold}VERDICT: TEST SUITE FAILED (${failedChecks} failures)${C.reset}\n`);
  process.exit(1);
} else {
  console.log(`\n${C.green}${C.bold}VERDICT: ALL ${totalChecks} AUTOMATED VERIFICATION CHECKS PASSED (100% SUCCESS)${C.reset}\n`);
  process.exit(0);
}
```

